        "name": "Triforce Panel",
        "_comment": "A Triforce cabinet (chimera#148): Sega's baseboard reads each player's panel as a GameCube pad and maps it to the game's JVS lines itself - which button is 'Shoot' or 'Pass' is the game's own adapter in dolphin (Virtua Striker, F-Zero AX, Mario Kart Arcade GP each differ). Two players, each a GameCube pad's twelve buttons and six axes, then the cabinet's Coin, Service and Test switches. Coin inserts a credit; Test opens the operator menu, which needs SegaBoot and is refused without it.",
